OL,1,Vk4                               G5/18
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGGORBACHEV REJECTS CALL TO
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCHANGE PARTY NAME
OL,4,D
OL,5, Soviet President Mikhail Gorbachev has
OL,6, rejected a call to change the name of
OL,7, the Soviet Communist Party, says TASS.
OL,9,FThe President told the party central
OL,10,Fcommittee that the move would seriously
OL,11,Fharm the communists' "ideological
OL,12,Ffoundation" and frustrate many members.
OL,14,FMr Gorbachev also proposed revamping
OL,15,Fthe Politburo into a Presidium to
OL,16,Finclude leaders of the republican
OL,17,Fcommunist parties.
OL,19,FTASS said he also proposed calling a
OL,20,Fspecial party congress on 2 July to
OL,21,Fcarry out these and other changes.
OL,23,D]FFromG11-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773236241
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/18
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGLITHUANIAN PARLIAMENT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGASSERTS SOVEREIGNTY
OL,4,D
OL,5, In the USSR, the parliament of the
OL,6, republic of Lithuania has voted for a
OL,7, declaration that the country's
OL,8, sovereignty has been "re-instated".
OL,10,FThis sovereignty was curtailed by
OL,11,Fforeign powers tn 1940, said the
OL,12,Fparliament's declaration - a reference
OL,13,Fto annexation by the USSR.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FEarlier, non-Communist Vytautas
OL,16,FLandsbergis, leader of the Sajudis
OL,17,Fnationalist movement, was elected
OL,18,Fpresident.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe republic's name has also been
OL,21,Fchanged, dropping the title "Soviet".
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG11-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
