OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGSCOTTISH LABOUR PARTY VOTE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGFOR UNILATERALISM
OL,5, The Scottish Labour party has voted for
OL,6, unilateral nuclear disarmament.
OL,8,FThe motion was passed by 358,000 votes
OL,9,Fto 322,000 at its conference in Dunoon.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FIt called for all nuclear weapons to be
OL,12,Fremoved from British soil and waters
OL,13,Fwithin the lifetime of a Labour
OL,14,Fgovernment.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FParty leader Neil Kinnock persuaded the
OL,17,FUK party to drop its unilateral policy
OL,18,Flast autumn.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe Scottish party said disarmament
OL,21,Fwould free money for social policies.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG11-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
